P18-V01 `querySubscriptionByConsumer` slice (2026-10-18 01:44 UTC)

## Scope and decision

- Continued the source-backed reconciliation of Java 5.5.1
  `client/MqClientAdmin.java` after `queryTopicsByConsumer`.
- Added the second method slice, `querySubscriptionByConsumer`. The broader
  P18-V01 audit remains open; 17 interface methods remain unreconciled.
- Kept the Java oracle at `/Users/bruce.tsai/Projects/3rd/rocketmq` read-only.
  Existing Phase 19 worktree changes in `integration-tests/`,
  `tests/differential/`, and its validation log were not staged.

## Implementation

- Added `QuerySubscriptionByConsumerRequestHeader` with nullable group, topic,
  and inherited topic-request fields; request code 345 is used by
  `MQClientApi::query_subscription_by_consumer`.
- Added `QuerySubscriptionResponseBody`, preserving Java's omitted-null JSON,
  nullable `SubscriptionData`, and getter alias. Added an invoked Java fixture
  for default/populated JSON, accessors, and nested-object identity.
- Extended Java/Rust header decode-mode fixtures for valid, missing, and
  malformed Boolean values under both decode hints. Added typed Java/Rust
  cross-decode fixtures and the missing public-header inventory/validation
  rows for both consumer-query headers.
- Added scripted Core RPC coverage for successful decoding, nullable response
  data, and Broker error mapping.
- Code commit: `2ac9351b feat(admin): add query subscription by consumer RPC`.

## Validation

Environment: macOS 26.6.1 aarch64, Rust/Cargo 1.85.0, Maven 3.10.0, Java 27.

- `cargo test --locked -p rocketmq-classic-protocol --all-features` — the first
  run exposed missing inventory and header-validation rows for the two
  `MqClientAdmin` request headers. After adding the rows, the full suite passed,
  including 130 unit tests, header inventory/validation, and 46 doctests.
- `cargo test --locked -p rocketmq-classic-remoting --all-features` — passed,
  including 137 unit tests, 107 transport tests, and 18 doctests.
- `cargo test --locked -p rocketmq-classic-core --all-features --test admin_rpc`
  — passed all 22 admin RPC tests.
- `mvn -q -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml verify` — passed 37 scenarios,
  fixture drift checks, and Java/Rust cross-decodes for 58 typed headers and
  14 typed bodies.
- `cargo clippy --locked -p rocketmq-classic-protocol
  -p rocketmq-classic-remoting -p rocketmq-classic-core --all-targets
  --all-features -- -D warnings` — passed.
- `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check` — passed.

